  "rendered_prompt": "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nParagraph:\n\"\"\"\nIn The Crucible, Arthur Miller shows how fear can make a whole town turn against itself. When a group of girls in Salem start accusing people of witchcraft, the adults believe them without asking for proof. Anyone who disagrees with the court is in danger of being accused too. John Proctor knows the girls are lying, but at first he is afraid to speak up because he has his own secret. In the end, he chooses to die rather than sign a false confession. Miller wrote the play in the 1950s to criticize the way people were being accused of being communists without real evidence.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer selected this text:\n\"\"\"\nMiller wrote the play in the 1950s to criticize the way people were being accused of being communists without real evidence.\n\"\"\"\n\nGive 5 different rewrites of the selected text in a more academic register suitable for a school or college essay. Keep the same meaning and the same level of certainty. Do not add evidence, statistics, names, citations or new ideas. Put the best options first.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n",
